5.1 ORDER-TO-TRADE RATIO (OTR)
-------------------------------
Definition: Count of order messages divided by number of trades produced.

Key exemption:
- Orders within ±40% of LTP for options premium, or ±₹20 (whichever is higher)
- These orders are excluded from OTR computation for penalty purposes

Purpose: OTR is a key metric for gauging algo-related activity.

REF: NSE Circulars; SEBI Guidelines

